# Target C: rank-density barrier through two no-root four-cycles

Date: 2026-09-20

Status: exact finite result for the global four-cycle metric-basis subproblem. This does not reduce the current 3,874-state generic-H6 endpoint and does not close C-II.

The companion verifier is

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_two_noroot_density_2026_09_20.py`.

## Statement

Use the notation of the relative four-cycle normal-form audit. Let `M` be the 85-dimensional four-cycle span modulo the 56 automatic side-triangle rows, let `T` be the 15-dimensional ground-root star space, and let `Q=M/T`. For a four-cycle family `A`, put

`delta(A) = r_M(A) - r_Q(A)`.

The verifier proves:

> If `A` contains at most two simple four-cycles avoiding root `0`, then
>
> `3 delta(A) <= |A|`.

Therefore, if `delta(A)=15`, then `|A|>=45`. In particular:

> Every hypothetical sufficient 44-cycle family must contain at least three four-cycles avoiding root `0`.

The committed 45-cycle family `F` consists entirely of cycles containing root `0`. Combining the new result with the already-certified seven-outsider exchange barrier gives a sharper description of any hypothetical 44-cycle replacement: it must use at least eight cycles outside `F`, and at least three of those outsiders must avoid root `0`.

This is still not a proof that 45 is globally minimal. Families with three or more no-root cycles remain untreated by this result.

## Exact coordinate model

The verifier rebuilds the complete 210-row four-cycle system from integer `L(K8)` cycle chains and performs all proof rank calculations over `Q` using `Fraction` arithmetic.

The 105 root-0 cycles split into 35 quotient blocks, one for each three-subset of `{1,...,7}`. In exact quotient coordinates, each block consists of the three vectors

`(1,0), (0,1), (1,-1)`.

Choosing the first two vectors in each block gives 70 quotient coordinates. Appending an exact 15-vector basis for `T` gives an 85-dimensional coordinate basis for `M`. Every one of the 210 four-cycle rows has integral coordinates in this basis, with all coefficients in

`{-2,-1,0,1,2}`.

Every no-root four-cycle has nonzero quotient components in exactly four blocks, the four triangular faces of its vertex four-set.

The verifier checks exactly

- `r_M=85`,
- `r_Q=70`,
- `dim T=15`,
- the 35 local block normal forms, and
- the four-block support of all 105 no-root cycles.

## Reduction to touched blocks

Fix a family with `t<=2` no-root cycles. Call a local block *touched* if one of those no-root cycles has a nonzero quotient component in that block.

Root-0 rows in untouched blocks decouple in `Q`. An incomplete untouched block contributes no relative direction. A complete untouched block uses three rows and can contribute at most one relative direction. Thus those blocks already satisfy the desired factor-three bound and can be removed from the hard part of the calculation.

Inside the touched blocks, write

- `c` for the number of complete three-row blocks,
- `p` for the number of selected root-0 rows in incomplete blocks, and
- `k` for the extra quotient nullity supplied by the `t` no-root rows after quotienting by the selected root-0 block spans.

A singleton incomplete block contributes one to `p`; a double contributes two; an empty block contributes zero. Complete blocks are counted in `c`, not `p`.

The local row count and quotient nullity are

`n = t + 3c + p`,

`K = c + k`.

The actual relative dimension `delta` is at most the quotient nullity `K`, so

`n - 3 delta >= n - 3K = t + p - 3k`.

Consequently only states with `t+p-3k<0` require an exact `M`-rank calculation. This leaves a small finite ledger.

## One no-root cycle

All 105 no-root cycles form one `S_7` orbit under relabeling of vertices `1,...,7`.

For `t=1`, a possible violation requires `k=1` and `p<=1`. Across the four touched blocks, exactly five root-0 selection states satisfy this crude condition.

All five are exactified over `Q`. None violates the rank-density inequality. The minimum exact defect is

`n - 3 delta = 2`.

## Two no-root cycles

The `C(105,2)=5460` unordered pairs of no-root cycles split into exactly seven `S_7` orbits. Their orbit sizes are

`105, 315, 630, 630, 1260, 1260, 1260`.

A pair touches 4, 7, or 8 local quotient blocks, depending on its orbit.

For `t=2`, a possible violation requires either

- `k=1` and `p=0`, or
- `k=2` and `p<=3`.

Enumerating only states with `p<=3` over one representative of each pair orbit gives the following exact ledger. Each record is

`(orbit size, touched blocks, states tested, crude-potential-negative states)`:

```text
(1260, 7,  36080, 185)
(1260, 8, 103168, 315)
( 315, 8, 103168, 315)
( 630, 8, 103168, 315)
(1260, 8, 103168, 315)
( 105, 4,   1072,  13)
( 630, 7,  36080, 226)
```

There are 1,684 crude-potential-negative states in total. Every one is reranked exactly in both `M` and `Q`. None violates the inequality. Again the minimum exact defect is

`n - 3 delta = 2`.

No floating-point or modular rank decision is used to reject one of these states.

